{
  "name": "Anonymize faces in videos dropped into a Google Drive folder",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "0b5d2c6e-1a01-4c1e-9d51-5a3c1d0a0001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 700,
        "color": 4,
        "content": "## Anonymize faces in videos from a Google Drive folder\n\n**Who it's for:** anyone who shares footage of other people — schools, event teams, agencies, public offices, researchers — and must blur faces first (GDPR).\n\n**What it does:** every video added to a Drive folder comes back into a second folder with every face mosaiced in every frame, in the same format and resolution. Location metadata is removed. Processing runs on blurwerk's own hardware in Germany.\n\n### How it works\n1. **New file in folder** checks the input folder every minute.\n2. **Is it a video?** skips anything that is not.\n3. **Download video** fetches the file.\n4. **Anonymize video** prices it from its own header, pays with prepaid credit, uploads it and waits for the result.\n5. **Finished?** sends the result to the output folder, or stops with the reason if it failed (a failed job is not charged).\n\n### Setup (5 minutes)\n1. Buy credit at [blurwerk.de/credit](https://blurwerk.de/credit?ref=n8n-template) and add the token as a **blurwerk API** credential.\n2. Connect **Google Drive** on the three Drive nodes.\n3. Pick the input folder in **New file in folder** and the output folder in **Upload to output folder**. Use two different folders.\n4. In **Anonymize video**, read and tick both declarations.\n5. Activate the workflow.\n\nSound is kept by default; set **Options → Audio** to *Disguise Voice* or *Mute* if voices must not be recognisable. Always check a result before publishing it."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b5d2c6e-1a01-4c1e-9d51-5a3c1d0a0002",
      "name": "Section: find new videos",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 660,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "### 1. Find new videos\nPolls the input folder. Other file types are ignored."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b5d2c6e-1a01-4c1e-9d51-5a3c1d0a0003",
      "name": "Section: anonymize",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        700,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 300,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "### 2. Anonymize\nWaits up to two hours. Processing takes about twice the video's length at 1080p."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b5d2c6e-1a01-4c1e-9d51-5a3c1d0a0004",
      "name": "Section: deliver",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1040,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 480,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "### 3. Deliver\nThe anonymized file keeps the original name with `_anonymized` added."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b5d2c6e-1a01-4c1e-9d51-5a3c1d0a0010",
      "name": "New file in folder",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDriveTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        60,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyMinute"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggerOn": "specificFolder",
        "folderToWatch": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "",
          "mode": "list"
        },
        "event": "fileCreated",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b5d2c6e-1a01-4c1e-9d51-5a3c1d0a0011",
      "name": "Is it a video?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        280,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 3
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "5d2f0a3e-7c7e-4a0b-9d0e-3f1c2b4a0011",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.mimeType }}",
              "rightValue": "video/",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "startsWith"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b5d2c6e-1a01-4c1e-9d51-5a3c1d0a0012",
